# ── Secrets — never commit ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This repository is public.
#
# .env holds OPENAI_API_KEY, and OPENAI_API_KEY_EVAL for the content-safeguard
# evaluation. Two keys on purpose: the BLOCK set fires violating prompts at the
# safety stack, and that traffic must not ride the account that serves children.
.env

# Teacher-team files hold team names AND their six-digit secret codes in
# plaintext. That code is the ONLY thing protecting a team's encrypted work
# (19.9 bits — see the entropy note in teacher.html), so a committed copy lets
# anyone overwrite those teams. Inherited from the deleted tests/.gitignore;
# kept because the rule is about the file shape, not about which evaluation made it.
teams.json
audit-*/
eval-*/

# ── Evaluation outputs ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Results are committed ON PURPOSE — they are evidence and must be reproducible
# by others. Tracked, not ignored: evaluations/scribe_contract/model_selection/,
# evaluations/scribe_contract/heldout_results/, and the journals, run configs, summaries and
# contact sheets under evaluations/content_safeguard/.
#
# Only the bulk per-trial images are excluded, by that directory's own
# .gitignore — ~1.3 GB across the two rounds. Nothing to add here.

# ── Manuscript ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The paper PDF stays OUT of this public repo by default. Posting an
# under-review manuscript is a decision about venue policy and preprint rights,
# not a housekeeping one -- delete this rule deliberately if you want it public.
*.pdf

# Hand-offs from co-authors: the patch and its covering note are transport, not
# repository content. Their contents land as commits; the carriers do not.
JACK_START_HERE.md
*.patch

# ── Per-machine tool state ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CLAUDE.md itself IS tracked -- it is the architecture doc, and it carries the
# warnings that are not derivable from the code (the parallel page arrays, the
# synchronous object:added history trap, the sync version lock). These two are
# the per-developer half: local permissions and personal scratch notes, which
# differ per machine and can carry paths or tokens.
#
# evaluations/scribe_contract/HELDOUT_PROTOCOL.md is NOT tool state despite the
# name -- it is the pre-registered protocol for the §4.1 evaluation, cited by
# evaluations/scribe_contract/heldout_results/PROTOCOL.md. It stays tracked.
.claude/
CLAUDE.local.md

# ── Machine noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
.DS_Store
.playwright-mcp/
